%%report account-by-type title: Accounts by type entity: Account chart: pie x: type y: records help: Client, owner, architect, subcontractor, supplier, JV partner or authority organization. How accounts divide across type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(type::text, '(unset)') AS type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report account-by-party-role title: Accounts by party role entity: Account chart: pie x: party_role y: records help: Client, owner, architect, subcontractor, supplier, JV partner or authority organization. How accounts divide across party role, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(party_role::text, '(unset)') AS party_role, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report account-by-qualification-status title: Accounts by qualification status entity: Account chart: pie x: qualification_status y: records help: Client, owner, architect, subcontractor, supplier, JV partner or authority organization. How accounts divide across qualification status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(qualification_status::text, '(unset)') AS qualification_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_account WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report contact-by-stakeholder-role title: Contacts by stakeholder role entity: Contact chart: pie x: stakeholder_role y: records help: Individual stakeholder associated with an organization. How contacts divide across stakeholder role, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(stakeholder_role::text, '(unset)') AS stakeholder_role, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_contact WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report contact-created-per-month title: Contacts created per month entity: Contact chart: line x: month y: records help: Individual stakeholder associated with an organization. New contacts per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_contact WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report contact-per-account title: Contacts per account entity: Contact chart: bar x: account y: records help: Individual stakeholder associated with an organization. Which account the most contacts belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS account, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_contact x LEFT JOIN bus_account p ON p.id = x.account_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report project-stakeholder-by-influence-level title: Project Stakeholders by influence level entity: ProjectStakeholder chart: pie x: influence_level y: records help: Many-to-many assignment of contacts and accounts to a project. How project stakeholders divide across influence level, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(influence_level::text, '(unset)') AS influence_level, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project_stakeholder WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report project-stakeholder-by-raci title: Project Stakeholders by raci entity: ProjectStakeholder chart: pie x: raci y: records help: Many-to-many assignment of contacts and accounts to a project. How project stakeholders divide across raci, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(raci::text, '(unset)') AS raci, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project_stakeholder WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report project-stakeholder-by-role title: Project Stakeholders by role entity: ProjectStakeholder chart: pie x: role y: records help: Many-to-many assignment of contacts and accounts to a project. How project stakeholders divide across role, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(role::text, '(unset)') AS role, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project_stakeholder WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report lead-by-status title: Leads by status entity: Lead chart: pie x: status y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. How leads divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report lead-by-lead-source title: Leads by lead source entity: Lead chart: pie x: lead_source y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. How leads divide across lead source, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(lead_source::text, '(unset)') AS lead_source, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report lead-by-region title: Leads by region entity: Lead chart: pie x: region y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. How leads divide across region, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(region::text, '(unset)') AS region, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report lead-lifecycle title: Lead lifecycle entity: Lead chart: bar x: state y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Where leads sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report lead-created-per-month title: Leads created per month entity: Lead chart: line x: month y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. New leads per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report lead-created-by-weekday title: Leads created by day of the week entity: Lead chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Which days leads are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report lead-changed-per-month title: Leads last changed per month entity: Lead chart: line x: month y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. How recently leads were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report lead-age-bands title: How recently leads were changed entity: Lead chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report lead-edit-churn title: How often leads are edited entity: Lead chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report lead-bid-due-date-per-month title: Leads by bid due date entity: Lead chart: line x: month y: records help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Leads grouped by the month of bid due date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', bid_due_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND bid_due_date IS NOT NULL AND bid_due_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND bid_due_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report lead-estimated-value-by-status title: Total estimated value by status entity: Lead chart: bar x: status y: total_estimated_value help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Leads added up on estimated value, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(estimated_value)::numeric, 2) AS total_estimated_value FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report lead-estimated-value-per-month title: Average estimated value per month entity: Lead chart: line x: month y: average_estimated_value help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. The average estimated value of leads created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(estimated_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_estimated_value FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report lead-largest-by-estimated-value title: The ten largest leads by estimated value entity: Lead chart: bar x: record y: estimated_value help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. The records with the highest estimated value; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT company::text AS record, estimated_value FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND estimated_value IS NOT NULL ORDER BY estimated_value DESC LIMIT 10
%%report lead-strategic-fit-score-by-status title: Total strategic fit score by status entity: Lead chart: bar x: status y: total_strategic_fit_score help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. Leads added up on strategic fit score, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(strategic_fit_score)::numeric, 2) AS total_strategic_fit_score FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report lead-strategic-fit-score-per-month title: Average strategic fit score per month entity: Lead chart: line x: month y: average_strategic_fit_score help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. The average strategic fit score of leads created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(strategic_fit_score)::numeric, 2) AS average_strategic_fit_score FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report lead-largest-by-strategic-fit-score title: The ten largest leads by strategic fit score entity: Lead chart: bar x: record y: strategic_fit_score help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. The records with the highest strategic fit score; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT company::text AS record, strategic_fit_score FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND strategic_fit_score IS NOT NULL ORDER BY strategic_fit_score DESC LIMIT 10
%%report lead-completeness title: How complete leads are entity: Lead chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Unqualified market or project inquiry. For each optional field, how many leads leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'project name' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_name IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'lead source', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE lead_source IS NULL) FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'estimated value', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE estimated_value IS NULL) FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'bid due date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE bid_due_date IS NULL) FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'region', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE region IS NULL) FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'strategic fit score', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE strategic_fit_score IS NULL) FROM bus_lead WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
