%%report opportunity-competitor-by-outcome title: Opportunity Competitors by outcome entity: OpportunityCompetitor chart: pie x: outcome y: records help: Competitor participation and win-loss intelligence. How opportunity competitors divide across outcome, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(outcome::text, '(unset)') AS outcome, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_opportunity_competitor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report opportunity-competitor-by-position title: Opportunity Competitors by position entity: OpportunityCompetitor chart: pie x: position y: records help: Competitor participation and win-loss intelligence. How opportunity competitors divide across position, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(position::text, '(unset)') AS position, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_opportunity_competitor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report opportunity-competitor-estimated-price-by-outcome title: Total estimated price by outcome entity: OpportunityCompetitor chart: bar x: outcome y: total_estimated_price help: Competitor participation and win-loss intelligence. Opportunity Competitors added up on estimated price, split by outcome, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(outcome::text, '(unset)') AS outcome, ROUND(SUM(estimated_price)::numeric, 2) AS total_estimated_price FROM bus_opportunity_competitor WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report rfp-by-status title: RFPs by status entity: RFP chart: pie x: status y: records help: Client solicitation and response control record. How rfps divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_rfp WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report rfp-by-submission-method title: RFPs by submission method entity: RFP chart: pie x: submission_method y: records help: Client solicitation and response control record. How rfps divide across submission method, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(submission_method::text, '(unset)') AS submission_method, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_rfp WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report rfp-lifecycle title: RFP lifecycle entity: RFP chart: bar x: state y: records help: Client solicitation and response control record. Where rfps sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_rfp WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report rfp-compliance-score-by-status title: Total compliance score by status entity: RFP chart: bar x: status y: total_compliance_score help: Client solicitation and response control record. RFPs added up on compliance score, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(compliance_score)::numeric, 2) AS total_compliance_score FROM bus_rfp WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report rfp-compliance-score-per-month title: Average compliance score per month entity: RFP chart: line x: month y: average_compliance_score help: Client solicitation and response control record. The average compliance score of rfps created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(compliance_score)::numeric, 2) AS average_compliance_score FROM bus_rfp WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report rfp-largest-by-compliance-score title: The ten largest rfps by compliance score entity: RFP chart: bar x: record y: compliance_score help: Client solicitation and response control record. The records with the highest compliance score; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT rfp_number::text AS record, compliance_score FROM bus_rfp WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND compliance_score IS NOT NULL ORDER BY compliance_score DESC LIMIT 10
