%%report project-by-project-type title: Projects by project type entity: Project chart: pie x: project_type y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. How projects divide across project type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(project_type::text, '(unset)') AS project_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report project-lifecycle title: Project lifecycle entity: Project chart: bar x: state y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Where projects sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report project-created-per-month title: Projects created per month entity: Project chart: line x: month y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. New projects per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-created-by-weekday title: Projects created by day of the week entity: Project chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Which days projects are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report project-changed-per-month title: Projects last changed per month entity: Project chart: line x: month y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. How recently projects were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-age-bands title: How recently projects were changed entity: Project chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report project-edit-churn title: How often projects are edited entity: Project chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report project-removed-per-month title: Projects removed per month entity: Project chart: line x: month y: removed help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Records withdrawn from use each month; a rising line means the register is being cleared faster than it is kept. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', deleted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS removed FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-start-date-per-month title: Projects by start date entity: Project chart: line x: month y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Projects grouped by the month of start date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', start_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND start_date IS NOT NULL AND start_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND start_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-finish-date-per-month title: Projects by finish date entity: Project chart: line x: month y: records help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Projects grouped by the month of finish date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', finish_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND finish_date IS NOT NULL AND finish_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND finish_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-contract-value-by-status title: Total contract value by status (Project) entity: Project chart: bar x: status y: total_contract_value help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. Projects added up on contract value, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(contract_value)::numeric, 2) AS total_contract_value FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report project-contract-value-per-month title: Average contract value per month (Project) entity: Project chart: line x: month y: average_contract_value help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. The average contract value of projects created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(contract_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_contract_value FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-largest-by-contract-value title: The ten largest projects by contract value entity: Project chart: bar x: record y: contract_value help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. The records with the highest contract value; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, contract_value FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND contract_value IS NOT NULL ORDER BY contract_value DESC LIMIT 10
%%report project-completeness title: How complete projects are entity: Project chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Construction project system-of-engagement record. For each optional field, how many projects leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'opportunity' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE opportunity_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'start date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE start_date IS NULL) FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'finish date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE finish_date IS NULL) FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'contract value', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE contract_value IS NULL) FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'erp project key', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE erp_project_key IS NULL) FROM bus_project WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
