%%report wbs-node-level-by-status title: Total level by status entity: WBSNode chart: bar x: status y: total_level help: Hierarchical work breakdown structure node. WBSNodes added up on level, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(level)::numeric, 2) AS total_level FROM bus_wbs_node WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report cost-code-by-cost-type title: Cost Codes by cost type entity: CostCode chart: pie x: cost_type y: records help: Enterprise cost classification structure. How cost codes divide across cost type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(cost_type::text, '(unset)') AS cost_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_cost_code WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report cost-code-created-per-month title: Cost Codes created per month entity: CostCode chart: line x: month y: records help: Enterprise cost classification structure. New cost codes per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_cost_code WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report cost-code-per-parent-code title: Cost Codes per parent code entity: CostCode chart: bar x: parent_code y: records help: Enterprise cost classification structure. Which parent code the most cost codes belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS parent_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_cost_code x LEFT JOIN bus_parent_code p ON p.id = x.parent_code_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report project-budget-original-budget-per-month title: Average original budget per month entity: ProjectBudget chart: line x: month y: average_original_budget help: Budget baseline and current control totals by WBS and cost code. The average original budget of project budgets created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(original_budget)::numeric, 2) AS average_original_budget FROM bus_project_budget WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-budget-approved-changes-per-month title: Average approved changes per month entity: ProjectBudget chart: line x: month y: average_approved_changes help: Budget baseline and current control totals by WBS and cost code. The average approved changes of project budgets created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(approved_changes)::numeric, 2) AS average_approved_changes FROM bus_project_budget WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report project-budget-current-budget-per-month title: Average current budget per month entity: ProjectBudget chart: line x: month y: average_current_budget help: Budget baseline and current control totals by WBS and cost code. The average current budget of project budgets created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(current_budget)::numeric, 2) AS average_current_budget FROM bus_project_budget WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report schedule-milestone-by-status title: Schedule Milestones by status entity: ScheduleMilestone chart: pie x: status y: records help: Selected executive and contractual milestones synchronized from scheduling tools. How schedule milestones divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_schedule_milestone WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report schedule-milestone-lifecycle title: Schedule Milestone lifecycle entity: ScheduleMilestone chart: bar x: state y: records help: Selected executive and contractual milestones synchronized from scheduling tools. Where schedule milestones sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_schedule_milestone WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report schedule-milestone-per-project title: Schedule Milestones per project entity: ScheduleMilestone chart: bar x: project y: records help: Selected executive and contractual milestones synchronized from scheduling tools. Which project the most schedule milestones belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS project, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_schedule_milestone x LEFT JOIN bus_project p ON p.id = x.project_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report risk-by-status title: Risks by status entity: Risk chart: pie x: status y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. How risks divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report risk-by-category title: Risks by category entity: Risk chart: pie x: category y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. How risks divide across category, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(category::text, '(unset)') AS category, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report risk-by-response title: Risks by response entity: Risk chart: pie x: response y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. How risks divide across response, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(response::text, '(unset)') AS response, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report risk-lifecycle title: Risk lifecycle entity: Risk chart: bar x: state y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. Where risks sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report risk-created-per-month title: Risks created per month entity: Risk chart: line x: month y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. New risks per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report risk-created-by-weekday title: Risks created by day of the week entity: Risk chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. Which days risks are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report risk-age-bands title: How recently risks were changed entity: Risk chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report risk-probability-by-status title: Total probability by status entity: Risk chart: bar x: status y: total_probability help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. Risks added up on probability, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(probability)::numeric, 2) AS total_probability FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report risk-probability-per-month title: Average probability per month (Risk) entity: Risk chart: line x: month y: average_probability help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. The average probability of risks created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(probability)::numeric, 2) AS average_probability FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report risk-largest-by-probability title: The ten largest risks by probability entity: Risk chart: bar x: record y: probability help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. The records with the highest probability; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT category::text AS record, probability FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND probability IS NOT NULL ORDER BY probability DESC LIMIT 10
%%report risk-impact-score-by-status title: Total impact score by status entity: Risk chart: bar x: status y: total_impact_score help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. Risks added up on impact score, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(impact_score)::numeric, 2) AS total_impact_score FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
