%%report risk-largest-by-impact-score title: The ten largest risks by impact score entity: Risk chart: bar x: record y: impact_score help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. The records with the highest impact score; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT category::text AS record, impact_score FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND impact_score IS NOT NULL ORDER BY impact_score DESC LIMIT 10
%%report risk-exposure-by-status title: Total exposure by status entity: Risk chart: bar x: status y: total_exposure help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. Risks added up on exposure, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(exposure)::numeric, 2) AS total_exposure FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report risk-exposure-per-month title: Average exposure per month entity: Risk chart: line x: month y: average_exposure help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. The average exposure of risks created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(exposure)::numeric, 2) AS average_exposure FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report risk-largest-by-exposure title: The ten largest risks by exposure entity: Risk chart: bar x: record y: exposure help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. The records with the highest exposure; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT category::text AS record, exposure FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND exposure IS NOT NULL ORDER BY exposure DESC LIMIT 10
%%report risk-completeness title: How complete risks are entity: Risk chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Project or portfolio threat and opportunity register. For each optional field, how many risks leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'project' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'opportunity', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE opportunity_id IS NULL) FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'response', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE response IS NULL) FROM bus_risk WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
