%%report submittal-required-on-site-date-per-month title: Submittals by required on site date entity: Submittal chart: line x: month y: records help: Shop drawing, product data, sample or method statement workflow. Submittals grouped by the month of required on site date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', required_on_site_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND required_on_site_date IS NOT NULL AND required_on_site_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND required_on_site_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report submittal-submitted-date-per-month title: Submittals by submitted date entity: Submittal chart: line x: month y: records help: Shop drawing, product data, sample or method statement workflow. Submittals grouped by the month of submitted date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', submitted_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND submitted_date IS NOT NULL AND submitted_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND submitted_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report submittal-per-project title: Submittals per project entity: Submittal chart: bar x: project y: records help: Shop drawing, product data, sample or method statement workflow. Which project the most submittals belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS project, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_submittal x LEFT JOIN bus_project p ON p.id = x.project_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report submittal-completeness title: How complete submittals are entity: Submittal chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Shop drawing, product data, sample or method statement workflow. For each optional field, how many submittals leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'specification section' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE specification_section IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'responsible contractor', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE responsible_contractor_id IS NULL) FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'required on site date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE required_on_site_date IS NULL) FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'submitted date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE submitted_date IS NULL) FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'revision', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE revision IS NULL) FROM bus_submittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report document-register-by-status title: Document Registers by status entity: DocumentRegister chart: pie x: status y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. How document registers divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report document-register-by-document-type title: Document Registers by document type entity: DocumentRegister chart: pie x: document_type y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. How document registers divide across document type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(document_type::text, '(unset)') AS document_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report document-register-by-discipline title: Document Registers by discipline entity: DocumentRegister chart: pie x: discipline y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. How document registers divide across discipline, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(discipline::text, '(unset)') AS discipline, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report document-register-lifecycle title: Document Register lifecycle entity: DocumentRegister chart: bar x: state y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. Where document registers sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report document-register-created-per-month title: Document Registers created per month entity: DocumentRegister chart: line x: month y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. New document registers per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report document-register-created-by-weekday title: Document Registers created by day of the week entity: DocumentRegister chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. Which days document registers are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report document-register-changed-per-month title: Document Registers last changed per month entity: DocumentRegister chart: line x: month y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. How recently document registers were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report document-register-age-bands title: How recently document registers were changed entity: DocumentRegister chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report document-register-completeness title: How complete document registers are entity: DocumentRegister chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Metadata and revision control for controlled project documents. For each optional field, how many document registers leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'discipline' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE discipline IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'content document', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE content_document_id IS NULL) FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'external repository key', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE external_repository_key IS NULL) FROM bus_document_register WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report transmittal-by-status title: Transmittals by status entity: Transmittal chart: pie x: status y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. How transmittals divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report transmittal-by-purpose title: Transmittals by purpose entity: Transmittal chart: pie x: purpose y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. How transmittals divide across purpose, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(purpose::text, '(unset)') AS purpose, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report transmittal-lifecycle title: Transmittal lifecycle entity: Transmittal chart: bar x: state y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. Where transmittals sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report transmittal-created-per-month title: Transmittals created per month entity: Transmittal chart: line x: month y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. New transmittals per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transmittal-created-by-weekday title: Transmittals created by day of the week entity: Transmittal chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. Which days transmittals are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report transmittal-changed-per-month title: Transmittals last changed per month entity: Transmittal chart: line x: month y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. How recently transmittals were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transmittal-age-bands title: How recently transmittals were changed entity: Transmittal chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report transmittal-issue-date-per-month title: Transmittals by issue date entity: Transmittal chart: line x: month y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. Transmittals grouped by the month of issue date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', issue_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND issue_date IS NOT NULL AND issue_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND issue_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transmittal-acknowledged-date-per-month title: Transmittals by acknowledged date entity: Transmittal chart: line x: month y: records help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. Transmittals grouped by the month of acknowledged date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', acknowledged_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND acknowledged_date IS NOT NULL AND acknowledged_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND acknowledged_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transmittal-completeness title: How complete transmittals are entity: Transmittal chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Formal issue of controlled documents to recipients. For each optional field, how many transmittals leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'recipient account' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE recipient_account_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'acknowledged date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE acknowledged_date IS NULL) FROM bus_transmittal WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report transmittal-item-created-per-month title: Transmittal Items created per month entity: TransmittalItem chart: line x: month y: records help: Document revision included in a transmittal. New transmittal items per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transmittal-item-age-bands title: How recently transmittal items were changed entity: TransmittalItem chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Document revision included in a transmittal. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report transmittal-item-copies-per-month title: Average copies per month entity: TransmittalItem chart: line x: month y: average_copies help: Document revision included in a transmittal. The average copies of transmittal items created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(copies)::numeric, 2) AS average_copies FROM bus_transmittal_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report transmittal-item-largest-by-copies title: The ten largest transmittal items by copies entity: TransmittalItem chart: bar x: record y: copies help: Document revision included in a transmittal. The records with the highest copies; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT revision_issued::text AS record, copies FROM bus_transmittal_item WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND copies IS NOT NULL ORDER BY copies DESC LIMIT 10
%%report transmittal-item-per-transmittal title: Transmittal Items per transmittal entity: TransmittalItem chart: bar x: transmittal y: records help: Document revision included in a transmittal. Which transmittal the most transmittal items belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.purpose::text, '(none)') AS transmittal, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal_item x LEFT JOIN bus_transmittal p ON p.id = x.transmittal_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report transmittal-item-copies-per-transmittal title: Total copies per transmittal entity: TransmittalItem chart: bar x: transmittal y: total_copies help: Document revision included in a transmittal. Transmittal Items added up on copies for each transmittal, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.purpose::text, '(none)') AS transmittal, ROUND(SUM(x.copies)::numeric, 2) AS total_copies FROM bus_transmittal_item x LEFT JOIN bus_transmittal p ON p.id = x.transmittal_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report transmittal-item-per-document-register title: Transmittal Items per document register entity: TransmittalItem chart: bar x: document_register y: records help: Document revision included in a transmittal. Which document register the most transmittal items belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.title::text, '(none)') AS document_register, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_transmittal_item x LEFT JOIN bus_document_register p ON p.id = x.document_register_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report transmittal-item-copies-per-document-register title: Total copies per document register entity: TransmittalItem chart: bar x: document_register y: total_copies help: Document revision included in a transmittal. Transmittal Items added up on copies for each document register, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.title::text, '(none)') AS document_register, ROUND(SUM(x.copies)::numeric, 2) AS total_copies FROM bus_transmittal_item x LEFT JOIN bus_document_register p ON p.id = x.document_register_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
