%%report safety-observation-created-by-weekday title: Safety Observations created by day of the week entity: SafetyObservation chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Which days safety observations are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report safety-observation-changed-per-month title: Safety Observations last changed per month entity: SafetyObservation chart: line x: month y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. How recently safety observations were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report safety-observation-age-bands title: How recently safety observations were changed entity: SafetyObservation chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report safety-observation-edit-churn title: How often safety observations are edited entity: SafetyObservation chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report safety-observation-removed-per-month title: Safety Observations removed per month entity: SafetyObservation chart: line x: month y: removed help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Records withdrawn from use each month; a rising line means the register is being cleared faster than it is kept. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', deleted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS removed FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report safety-observation-observation-date-per-month title: Safety Observations by observation date entity: SafetyObservation chart: line x: month y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Safety Observations grouped by the month of observation date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', observation_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND observation_date IS NOT NULL AND observation_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND observation_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report safety-observation-due-date-per-month title: Safety Observations by due date entity: SafetyObservation chart: line x: month y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Safety Observations grouped by the month of due date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', due_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND due_date IS NOT NULL AND due_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND due_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report safety-observation-per-project title: Safety Observations per project entity: SafetyObservation chart: bar x: project y: records help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. Which project the most safety observations belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS project, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_safety_observation x LEFT JOIN bus_project p ON p.id = x.project_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report safety-observation-completeness title: How complete safety observations are entity: SafetyObservation chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Positive observation, hazard or unsafe act or condition. For each optional field, how many safety observations leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'immediate action' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE immediate_action IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'owner', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE owner_id IS NULL) FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'due date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE due_date IS NULL) FROM bus_safety_observation WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report permit-to-work-by-status title: Permit To Works by status entity: PermitToWork chart: pie x: status y: records help: Controlled authorization for hazardous work. How permit to works divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_permit_to_work WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report permit-to-work-by-permit-type title: Permit To Works by permit type entity: PermitToWork chart: pie x: permit_type y: records help: Controlled authorization for hazardous work. How permit to works divide across permit type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(permit_type::text, '(unset)') AS permit_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_permit_to_work WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report permit-to-work-lifecycle title: Permit To Work lifecycle entity: PermitToWork chart: bar x: state y: records help: Controlled authorization for hazardous work. Where permit to works sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_permit_to_work WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report resource-by-resource-type title: Resources by resource type entity: Resource chart: pie x: resource_type y: records help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. How resources divide across resource type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(resource_type::text, '(unset)') AS resource_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report resource-by-availability-status title: Resources by availability status entity: Resource chart: pie x: availability_status y: records help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. How resources divide across availability status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(availability_status::text, '(unset)') AS availability_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report resource-by-home-region title: Resources by home region entity: Resource chart: pie x: home_region y: records help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. How resources divide across home region, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(home_region::text, '(unset)') AS home_region, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report resource-created-per-month title: Resources created per month entity: Resource chart: line x: month y: records help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. New resources per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report resource-active-share title: Resources: active entity: Resource chart: pie x: active y: records help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. The share of resources where active holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN active THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS active, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report resource-cost-rate-by-resource-type title: Total cost rate by resource type entity: Resource chart: bar x: resource_type y: total_cost_rate help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. Resources added up on cost rate, split by resource type, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(resource_type::text, '(unset)') AS resource_type, ROUND(SUM(cost_rate)::numeric, 2) AS total_cost_rate FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report resource-cost-rate-per-month title: Average cost rate per month entity: Resource chart: line x: month y: average_cost_rate help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. The average cost rate of resources created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(cost_rate)::numeric, 2) AS average_cost_rate FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report resource-largest-by-cost-rate title: The ten largest resources by cost rate entity: Resource chart: bar x: record y: cost_rate help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. The records with the highest cost rate; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, cost_rate FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND cost_rate IS NOT NULL ORDER BY cost_rate DESC LIMIT 10
%%report resource-completeness title: How complete resources are entity: Resource chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Person, crew or capacity pool deployable to projects. For each optional field, how many resources leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'user' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE user_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'employer account', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE employer_account_id IS NULL) FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'home region', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE home_region IS NULL) FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'cost rate', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE cost_rate IS NULL) FROM bus_resource WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
