%%report equipment-assignment-start-date-per-month title: Equipment Assignments by start date entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: line x: month y: records help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. Equipment Assignments grouped by the month of start date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', start_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_equipment_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND start_date IS NOT NULL AND start_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND start_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report equipment-assignment-end-date-per-month title: Equipment Assignments by end date entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: line x: month y: records help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. Equipment Assignments grouped by the month of end date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', end_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_equipment_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND end_date IS NOT NULL AND end_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND end_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report equipment-assignment-daily-rate-by-status title: Total daily rate by status entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: bar x: status y: total_daily_rate help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. Equipment Assignments added up on daily rate, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(daily_rate)::numeric, 2) AS total_daily_rate FROM bus_equipment_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report equipment-assignment-daily-rate-per-month title: Average daily rate per month entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: line x: month y: average_daily_rate help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. The average daily rate of equipment assignments created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(daily_rate)::numeric, 2) AS average_daily_rate FROM bus_equipment_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report equipment-assignment-largest-by-daily-rate title: The ten largest equipment assignments by daily rate entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: bar x: record y: daily_rate help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. The records with the highest daily rate; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT status::text AS record, daily_rate FROM bus_equipment_assignment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND daily_rate IS NOT NULL ORDER BY daily_rate DESC LIMIT 10
%%report equipment-assignment-per-asset title: Equipment Assignments per asset entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: bar x: asset y: records help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. Which asset the most equipment assignments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS asset, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_equipment_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_asset p ON p.id = x.asset_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report equipment-assignment-daily-rate-per-asset title: Total daily rate per asset entity: EquipmentAssignment chart: bar x: asset y: total_daily_rate help: Assignment of equipment to project, site and period. Equipment Assignments added up on daily rate for each asset, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS asset, ROUND(SUM(x.daily_rate)::numeric, 2) AS total_daily_rate FROM bus_equipment_assignment x LEFT JOIN bus_asset p ON p.id = x.asset_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report work-order-by-status title: Work Orders by status entity: WorkOrder chart: pie x: status y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. How work orders divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report work-order-by-priority title: Work Orders by priority entity: WorkOrder chart: pie x: priority y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. How work orders divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report work-order-lifecycle title: Work Order lifecycle entity: WorkOrder chart: bar x: state y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. Where work orders sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report work-order-created-per-month title: Work Orders created per month entity: WorkOrder chart: line x: month y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. New work orders per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report work-order-age-bands title: How recently work orders were changed entity: WorkOrder chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report work-order-start-date-per-month title: Work Orders by start date entity: WorkOrder chart: line x: month y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. Work Orders grouped by the month of start date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', start_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND start_date IS NOT NULL AND start_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND start_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report work-order-end-date-per-month title: Work Orders by end date entity: WorkOrder chart: line x: month y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. Work Orders grouped by the month of end date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', end_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND end_date IS NOT NULL AND end_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND end_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report work-order-per-case title: Work Orders per case entity: WorkOrder chart: bar x: case y: records help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. Which case the most work orders belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.subject::text, '(none)') AS case, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_work_order x LEFT JOIN bus_case p ON p.id = x.case_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report work-order-completeness title: How complete work orders are entity: WorkOrder chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Corrective or preventive field work after or during delivery. For each optional field, how many work orders leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'account' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE account_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'asset', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE asset_id IS NULL) FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'case', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE case_id IS NULL) FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'project', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'work type', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE work_type_id IS NULL) FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'start date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE start_date IS NULL) FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'end date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE end_date IS NULL) FROM bus_work_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
