%%report warranty-created-per-month title: Warranties created per month entity: Warranty chart: line x: month y: records help: Warranty coverage for project scope or asset. New warranties per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report warranty-start-date-per-month title: Warranties by start date entity: Warranty chart: line x: month y: records help: Warranty coverage for project scope or asset. Warranties grouped by the month of start date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', start_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND start_date IS NOT NULL AND start_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND start_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report warranty-end-date-per-month title: Warranties by end date entity: Warranty chart: line x: month y: records help: Warranty coverage for project scope or asset. Warranties grouped by the month of end date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', end_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND end_date IS NOT NULL AND end_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND end_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report warranty-completeness title: How complete warranties are entity: Warranty chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Warranty coverage for project scope or asset. For each optional field, how many warranties leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'project' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'asset', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE asset_id IS NULL) FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'contract', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE contract_id IS NULL) FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'provider account', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE provider_account_id IS NULL) FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'terms', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE terms IS NULL) FROM bus_warranty WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report commissioning-system-by-status title: Commissioning Systems by status entity: CommissioningSystem chart: pie x: status y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. How commissioning systems divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report commissioning-system-lifecycle title: Commissioning System lifecycle entity: CommissioningSystem chart: bar x: state y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Where commissioning systems sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report commissioning-system-created-per-month title: Commissioning Systems created per month entity: CommissioningSystem chart: line x: month y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. New commissioning systems per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report commissioning-system-created-by-weekday title: Commissioning Systems created by day of the week entity: CommissioningSystem chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Which days commissioning systems are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report commissioning-system-changed-per-month title: Commissioning Systems last changed per month entity: CommissioningSystem chart: line x: month y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. How recently commissioning systems were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report commissioning-system-age-bands title: How recently commissioning systems were changed entity: CommissioningSystem chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report commissioning-system-edit-churn title: How often commissioning systems are edited entity: CommissioningSystem chart: bar x: edits y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report commissioning-system-planned-ready-date-per-month title: Commissioning Systems by planned ready date entity: CommissioningSystem chart: line x: month y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Commissioning Systems grouped by the month of planned ready date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', planned_ready_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND planned_ready_date IS NOT NULL AND planned_ready_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND planned_ready_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report commissioning-system-actual-ready-date-per-month title: Commissioning Systems by actual ready date entity: CommissioningSystem chart: line x: month y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Commissioning Systems grouped by the month of actual ready date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', actual_ready_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND actual_ready_date IS NOT NULL AND actual_ready_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND actual_ready_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report commissioning-system-per-project title: Commissioning Systems per project entity: CommissioningSystem chart: bar x: project y: records help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. Which project the most commissioning systems belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS project, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_commissioning_system x LEFT JOIN bus_project p ON p.id = x.project_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report commissioning-system-completeness title: How complete commissioning systems are entity: CommissioningSystem chart: bar x: field y: missing help: System or subsystem boundary used for commissioning. For each optional field, how many commissioning systems leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'parent system' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE parent_system_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'responsible account', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE responsible_account_id IS NULL) FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'planned ready date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE planned_ready_date IS NULL) FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'actual ready date', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE actual_ready_date IS NULL) FROM bus_commissioning_system WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
