%%report training-record-age-bands title: How recently training records were changed entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report training-record-edit-churn title: How often training records are edited entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report training-record-delivery-date-per-month title: Training Records by delivery date entity: TrainingRecord chart: line x: month y: records help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. Training Records grouped by the month of delivery date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', delivery_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND delivery_date IS NOT NULL AND delivery_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND delivery_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report training-record-attendance-count-per-month title: Average attendance count per month entity: TrainingRecord chart: line x: month y: average_attendance_count help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. The average attendance count of training records created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(attendance_count)::numeric, 2) AS average_attendance_count FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report training-record-largest-by-attendance-count title: The ten largest training records by attendance count entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: record y: attendance_count help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. The records with the highest attendance count; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT course_title::text AS record, attendance_count FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND attendance_count IS NOT NULL ORDER BY attendance_count DESC LIMIT 10
%%report training-record-per-project title: Training Records per project entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: project y: records help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. Which project the most training records belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS project, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_training_record x LEFT JOIN bus_project p ON p.id = x.project_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report training-record-per-commissioning-system title: Training Records per commissioning system entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: commissioning_system y: records help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. Which commissioning system the most training records belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS commissioning_system, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_training_record x LEFT JOIN bus_commissioning_system p ON p.id = x.commissioning_system_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report training-record-attendance-count-per-commissioning-system title: Total attendance count per commissioning system entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: commissioning_system y: total_attendance_count help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. Training Records added up on attendance count for each commissioning system, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS commissioning_system, ROUND(SUM(x.attendance_count)::numeric, 2) AS total_attendance_count FROM bus_training_record x LEFT JOIN bus_commissioning_system p ON p.id = x.commissioning_system_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report training-record-completeness title: How complete training records are entity: TrainingRecord chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Operational training delivered to client or facility team. For each optional field, how many training records leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'commissioning system' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE commissioning_system_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'trainer', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE trainer_id IS NULL) FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'recipient account', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE recipient_account_id IS NULL) FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'attendance count', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE attendance_count IS NULL) FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'evidence file', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE evidence_file_id IS NULL) FROM bus_training_record WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report procurement-request-by-approval-status title: Procurement Requests by approval status entity: ProcurementRequest chart: pie x: approval_status y: records help: Approved request sent to ERP or procurement system. How procurement requests divide across approval status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(approval_status::text, '(unset)') AS approval_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_procurement_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report procurement-request-estimated-value-by-approval-status title: Total estimated value by approval status entity: ProcurementRequest chart: bar x: approval_status y: total_estimated_value help: Approved request sent to ERP or procurement system. Procurement Requests added up on estimated value, split by approval status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(approval_status::text, '(unset)') AS approval_status, ROUND(SUM(estimated_value)::numeric, 2) AS total_estimated_value FROM bus_procurement_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report procurement-request-estimated-value-per-month title: Average estimated value per month (Procurement Request) entity: ProcurementRequest chart: line x: month y: average_estimated_value help: Approved request sent to ERP or procurement system. The average estimated value of procurement requests created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(estimated_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_estimated_value FROM bus_procurement_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report purchase-order-summary-by-status title: Purchase Order Summaries by status entity: PurchaseOrderSummary chart: pie x: status y: records help: Read-only operational summary from ERP. How purchase order summaries divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_purchase_order_summary WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report purchase-order-summary-lifecycle title: Purchase Order Summary lifecycle entity: PurchaseOrderSummary chart: bar x: state y: records help: Read-only operational summary from ERP. Where purchase order summaries sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_purchase_order_summary WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report purchase-order-summary-original-value-by-status title: Total original value by status entity: PurchaseOrderSummary chart: bar x: status y: total_original_value help: Read-only operational summary from ERP. Purchase Order Summaries added up on original value, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(original_value)::numeric, 2) AS total_original_value FROM bus_purchase_order_summary WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
