%%report journal-entry-created-per-month title: Journal Entries created per month entity: JournalEntry chart: line x: month y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. New journal entries per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-entry-created-by-weekday title: Journal Entries created by day of the week entity: JournalEntry chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. Which days journal entries are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report journal-entry-changed-per-month title: Journal Entries last changed per month entity: JournalEntry chart: line x: month y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. How recently journal entries were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-entry-age-bands title: How recently journal entries were changed entity: JournalEntry chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report journal-entry-accounting-date-per-month title: Journal Entries by accounting date entity: JournalEntry chart: line x: month y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. Journal Entries grouped by the month of accounting date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', accounting_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND accounting_date IS NOT NULL AND accounting_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND accounting_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-entry-posted-at-per-month title: Journal Entries by posted at entity: JournalEntry chart: line x: month y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. Journal Entries grouped by the month of posted at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', posted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND posted_at IS NOT NULL AND posted_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND posted_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-entry-top-currency-code title: Journal Entries: the most common currency code entity: JournalEntry chart: bar x: currency_code y: records help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. The ten most frequent values of currency code among journal entries; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency_code, '(blank)') AS currency_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report journal-entry-completeness title: How complete journal entries are entity: JournalEntry chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Balanced accounting document posted to a ledger and period. For each optional field, how many journal entries leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'reversal journal' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE reversal_journal_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'posted at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE posted_at IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_entry WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report journal-line-created-per-month title: Journal Lines created per month entity: JournalLine chart: line x: month y: records help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. New journal lines per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-line-created-by-weekday title: Journal Lines created by day of the week entity: JournalLine chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. Which days journal lines are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report journal-line-changed-per-month title: Journal Lines last changed per month entity: JournalLine chart: line x: month y: records help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. How recently journal lines were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-line-age-bands title: How recently journal lines were changed entity: JournalLine chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report journal-line-debit-amount-per-month title: Average debit amount per month entity: JournalLine chart: line x: month y: average_debit_amount help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. The average debit amount of journal lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(debit_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_debit_amount FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-line-credit-amount-per-month title: Average credit amount per month entity: JournalLine chart: line x: month y: average_credit_amount help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. The average credit amount of journal lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(credit_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_credit_amount FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-line-entered-amount-per-month title: Average entered amount per month entity: JournalLine chart: line x: month y: average_entered_amount help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. The average entered amount of journal lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(entered_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_entered_amount FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report journal-line-per-journal-entry title: Journal Lines per journal entry entity: JournalLine chart: bar x: journal_entry y: records help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. Which journal entry the most journal lines belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.journal_number::text, '(none)') AS journal_entry, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_journal_line x LEFT JOIN bus_journal_entry p ON p.id = x.journal_entry_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report journal-line-debit-amount-per-journal-entry title: Total debit amount per journal entry entity: JournalLine chart: bar x: journal_entry y: total_debit_amount help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. Journal Lines added up on debit amount for each journal entry, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.journal_number::text, '(none)') AS journal_entry, ROUND(SUM(x.debit_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_debit_amount FROM bus_journal_line x LEFT JOIN bus_journal_entry p ON p.id = x.journal_entry_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report journal-line-completeness title: How complete journal lines are entity: JournalLine chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Debit or credit line with dimensional accounting distribution. For each optional field, how many journal lines leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'debit amount' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE debit_amount IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'credit amount', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE credit_amount IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'project', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'wbs node', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE wbs_node_id IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'cost code', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE cost_code_id IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'cost center', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE cost_center_id IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'source transaction', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE source_transaction_id IS NULL) FROM bus_journal_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
