%%report goods-receipt-created-by-weekday title: Goods Receipts created by day of the week entity: GoodsReceipt chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Which days goods receipts are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report goods-receipt-changed-per-month title: Goods Receipts last changed per month entity: GoodsReceipt chart: line x: month y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. How recently goods receipts were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report goods-receipt-age-bands title: How recently goods receipts were changed entity: GoodsReceipt chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report goods-receipt-edit-churn title: How often goods receipts are edited entity: GoodsReceipt chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report goods-receipt-removed-per-month title: Goods Receipts removed per month entity: GoodsReceipt chart: line x: month y: removed help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Records withdrawn from use each month; a rising line means the register is being cleared faster than it is kept. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', deleted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS removed FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report goods-receipt-receipt-date-per-month title: Goods Receipts by receipt date entity: GoodsReceipt chart: line x: month y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Goods Receipts grouped by the month of receipt date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', receipt_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND receipt_date IS NOT NULL AND receipt_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND receipt_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report goods-receipt-per-purchase-order title: Goods Receipts per purchase order entity: GoodsReceipt chart: bar x: purchase_order y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Which purchase order the most goods receipts belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.po_number::text, '(none)') AS purchase_order, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt x LEFT JOIN bus_purchase_order p ON p.id = x.purchase_order_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report goods-receipt-per-warehouse title: Goods Receipts per warehouse entity: GoodsReceipt chart: bar x: warehouse y: records help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. Which warehouse the most goods receipts belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.code::text, '(none)') AS warehouse, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt x LEFT JOIN bus_warehouse p ON p.id = x.warehouse_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report goods-receipt-completeness title: How complete goods receipts are entity: GoodsReceipt chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Receipt and acceptance of goods or services against an order. For each optional field, how many goods receipts leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'warehouse' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE warehouse_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'project', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) FROM bus_goods_receipt WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report goods-receipt-line-by-inspection-status title: Goods Receipt Lines by inspection status entity: GoodsReceiptLine chart: pie x: inspection_status y: records help: Quantity and valuation received for a purchase-order line. How goods receipt lines divide across inspection status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(inspection_status::text, '(unset)') AS inspection_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_goods_receipt_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report goods-receipt-line-quantity-received-by-inspection-status title: Total quantity received by inspection status entity: GoodsReceiptLine chart: bar x: inspection_status y: total_quantity_received help: Quantity and valuation received for a purchase-order line. Goods Receipt Lines added up on quantity received, split by inspection status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(inspection_status::text, '(unset)') AS inspection_status, ROUND(SUM(quantity_received)::numeric, 2) AS total_quantity_received FROM bus_goods_receipt_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report goods-receipt-line-quantity-received-per-month title: Average quantity received per month entity: GoodsReceiptLine chart: line x: month y: average_quantity_received help: Quantity and valuation received for a purchase-order line. The average quantity received of goods receipt lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quantity_received)::numeric, 2) AS average_quantity_received FROM bus_goods_receipt_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report supplier-invoice-by-approval-status title: Supplier Invoices by approval status entity: SupplierInvoice chart: pie x: approval_status y: records help: Accounts payable invoice or credit memo. How supplier invoices divide across approval status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(approval_status::text, '(unset)') AS approval_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report supplier-invoice-by-match-status title: Supplier Invoices by match status entity: SupplierInvoice chart: pie x: match_status y: records help: Accounts payable invoice or credit memo. How supplier invoices divide across match status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(match_status::text, '(unset)') AS match_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report supplier-invoice-by-payment-status title: Supplier Invoices by payment status entity: SupplierInvoice chart: pie x: payment_status y: records help: Accounts payable invoice or credit memo. How supplier invoices divide across payment status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(payment_status::text, '(unset)') AS payment_status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report supplier-invoice-top-currency-code title: Supplier Invoices: the most common currency code entity: SupplierInvoice chart: bar x: currency_code y: records help: Accounts payable invoice or credit memo. The ten most frequent values of currency code among supplier invoices; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency_code, '(blank)') AS currency_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report supplier-invoice-line-quantity-per-month title: Average quantity per month (Supplier Invoice Line) entity: SupplierInvoiceLine chart: line x: month y: average_quantity help: Invoice line and project cost distribution. The average quantity of supplier invoice lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_quantity FROM bus_supplier_invoice_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report supplier-invoice-line-largest-by-quantity title: The ten largest supplier invoice lines by quantity entity: SupplierInvoiceLine chart: bar x: record y: quantity help: Invoice line and project cost distribution. The records with the highest quantity; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT tax_code::text AS record, quantity FROM bus_supplier_invoice_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND quantity IS NOT NULL ORDER BY quantity DESC LIMIT 10
%%report supplier-invoice-line-unit-price-per-month title: Average unit price per month (Supplier Invoice Line) entity: SupplierInvoiceLine chart: line x: month y: average_unit_price help: Invoice line and project cost distribution. The average unit price of supplier invoice lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(unit_price)::numeric, 2) AS average_unit_price FROM bus_supplier_invoice_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report supplier-payment-by-status title: Supplier Payments by status entity: SupplierPayment chart: pie x: status y: records help: Payment to supplier with invoice applications. How supplier payments divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_payment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report supplier-payment-by-payment-method title: Supplier Payments by payment method entity: SupplierPayment chart: pie x: payment_method y: records help: Payment to supplier with invoice applications. How supplier payments divide across payment method, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(payment_method::text, '(unset)') AS payment_method, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_payment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report supplier-payment-lifecycle title: Supplier Payment lifecycle entity: SupplierPayment chart: bar x: state y: records help: Payment to supplier with invoice applications. Where supplier payments sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_payment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report supplier-payment-top-currency-code title: Supplier Payments: the most common currency code entity: SupplierPayment chart: bar x: currency_code y: records help: Payment to supplier with invoice applications. The ten most frequent values of currency code among supplier payments; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency_code, '(blank)') AS currency_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_supplier_payment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
