%%report customer-invoice-retention-amount-by-status title: Total retention amount by status entity: CustomerInvoice chart: bar x: status y: total_retention_amount help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. Customer Invoices added up on retention amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(retention_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_retention_amount FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report customer-invoice-retention-amount-per-month title: Average retention amount per month (Customer Invoice) entity: CustomerInvoice chart: line x: month y: average_retention_amount help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. The average retention amount of customer invoices created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(retention_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_retention_amount FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report customer-invoice-largest-by-retention-amount title: The ten largest customer invoices by retention amount entity: CustomerInvoice chart: bar x: record y: retention_amount help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. The records with the highest retention amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT invoice_number::text AS record, retention_amount FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND retention_amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY retention_amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report customer-invoice-tax-amount-by-status title: Total tax amount by status entity: CustomerInvoice chart: bar x: status y: total_tax_amount help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. Customer Invoices added up on tax amount, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(tax_amount)::numeric, 2) AS total_tax_amount FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report customer-invoice-tax-amount-per-month title: Average tax amount per month (Customer Invoice) entity: CustomerInvoice chart: line x: month y: average_tax_amount help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. The average tax amount of customer invoices created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(tax_amount)::numeric, 2) AS average_tax_amount FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report customer-invoice-largest-by-tax-amount title: The ten largest customer invoices by tax amount entity: CustomerInvoice chart: bar x: record y: tax_amount help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. The records with the highest tax amount; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT invoice_number::text AS record, tax_amount FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND tax_amount IS NOT NULL ORDER BY tax_amount DESC LIMIT 10
%%report customer-invoice-top-currency-code title: Customer Invoices: the most common currency code entity: CustomerInvoice chart: bar x: currency_code y: records help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. The ten most frequent values of currency code among customer invoices; free text that repeats is a list the model could close. sql: SELECT COALESCE(currency_code, '(blank)') AS currency_code, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report customer-invoice-completeness title: How complete customer invoices are entity: CustomerInvoice chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Accounts receivable progress invoice, milestone invoice or credit memo. For each optional field, how many customer invoices leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'customer contract' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE customer_contract_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'project', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'retention amount', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE retention_amount IS NULL) FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'tax amount', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE tax_amount IS NULL) FROM bus_customer_invoice WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report customer-invoice-line-quantity-per-month title: Average quantity per month (Customer Invoice Line) entity: CustomerInvoiceLine chart: line x: month y: average_quantity help: Billable line mapped to SOV, project, revenue and tax. The average quantity of customer invoice lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_quantity FROM bus_customer_invoice_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
