%%report timesheet-by-status title: Timesheets by status entity: Timesheet chart: pie x: status y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. How timesheets divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report timesheet-lifecycle title: Timesheet lifecycle entity: Timesheet chart: bar x: state y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Where timesheets sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'active', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 3) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report timesheet-created-per-month title: Timesheets created per month entity: Timesheet chart: line x: month y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. New timesheets per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-created-by-weekday title: Timesheets created by day of the week entity: Timesheet chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Which days timesheets are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report timesheet-changed-per-month title: Timesheets last changed per month entity: Timesheet chart: line x: month y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. How recently timesheets were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-age-bands title: How recently timesheets were changed entity: Timesheet chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report timesheet-edit-churn title: How often timesheets are edited entity: Timesheet chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report timesheet-week-ending-date-per-month title: Timesheets by week ending date entity: Timesheet chart: line x: month y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Timesheets grouped by the month of week ending date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', week_ending_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND week_ending_date IS NOT NULL AND week_ending_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND week_ending_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-submitted-at-per-month title: Timesheets by submitted at entity: Timesheet chart: line x: month y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Timesheets grouped by the month of submitted at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', submitted_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND submitted_at IS NOT NULL AND submitted_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND submitted_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-approved-at-per-month title: Timesheets by approved at entity: Timesheet chart: line x: month y: records help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. Timesheets grouped by the month of approved at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', approved_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND approved_at IS NOT NULL AND approved_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND approved_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-completeness title: How complete timesheets are entity: Timesheet chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Worker time submission for project, payroll and cost. For each optional field, how many timesheets leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'submitted at' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE submitted_at IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'approved by', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE approved_by_id IS NULL) FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'approved at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE approved_at IS NULL) FROM bus_timesheet WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report timesheet-line-created-per-month title: Timesheet Lines created per month entity: TimesheetLine chart: line x: month y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. New timesheet lines per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-line-created-by-weekday title: Timesheet Lines created by day of the week entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: weekday y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. Which days timesheet lines are recorded on, which is the working rhythm of the people who enter them. sql: SELECT to_char(created_at, 'Dy') AS weekday, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1, EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at) ORDER BY EXTRACT(isodow FROM created_at)
%%report timesheet-line-changed-per-month title: Timesheet Lines last changed per month entity: TimesheetLine chart: line x: month y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. How recently timesheet lines were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-line-age-bands title: How recently timesheet lines were changed entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report timesheet-line-work-date-per-month title: Timesheet Lines by work date entity: TimesheetLine chart: line x: month y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. Timesheet Lines grouped by the month of work date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', work_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND work_date IS NOT NULL AND work_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND work_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-line-billable-share title: Timesheet Lines: billable entity: TimesheetLine chart: pie x: billable y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The share of timesheet lines where billable holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN billable THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS billable, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report timesheet-line-hours-per-month title: Average hours per month entity: TimesheetLine chart: line x: month y: average_hours help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The average hours of timesheet lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(hours)::numeric, 2) AS average_hours FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-line-largest-by-hours title: The ten largest timesheet lines by hours entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: record y: hours help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The records with the highest hours; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT pay_code::text AS record, hours FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND hours IS NOT NULL ORDER BY hours DESC LIMIT 10
%%report timesheet-line-labor-rate-per-month title: Average labor rate per month entity: TimesheetLine chart: line x: month y: average_labor_rate help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The average labor rate of timesheet lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(labor_rate)::numeric, 2) AS average_labor_rate FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-line-largest-by-labor-rate title: The ten largest timesheet lines by labor rate entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: record y: labor_rate help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The records with the highest labor rate; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT pay_code::text AS record, labor_rate FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND labor_rate IS NOT NULL ORDER BY labor_rate DESC LIMIT 10
%%report timesheet-line-labor-cost-per-month title: Average labor cost per month entity: TimesheetLine chart: line x: month y: average_labor_cost help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The average labor cost of timesheet lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(labor_cost)::numeric, 2) AS average_labor_cost FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report timesheet-line-largest-by-labor-cost title: The ten largest timesheet lines by labor cost entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: record y: labor_cost help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. The records with the highest labor cost; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT pay_code::text AS record, labor_cost FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND labor_cost IS NOT NULL ORDER BY labor_cost DESC LIMIT 10
%%report timesheet-line-per-timesheet title: Timesheet Lines per timesheet entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: timesheet y: records help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. Which timesheet the most timesheet lines belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.status::text, '(none)') AS timesheet, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_timesheet_line x LEFT JOIN bus_timesheet p ON p.id = x.timesheet_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report timesheet-line-hours-per-timesheet title: Total hours per timesheet entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: timesheet y: total_hours help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. Timesheet Lines added up on hours for each timesheet, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.status::text, '(none)') AS timesheet, ROUND(SUM(x.hours)::numeric, 2) AS total_hours FROM bus_timesheet_line x LEFT JOIN bus_timesheet p ON p.id = x.timesheet_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report timesheet-line-completeness title: How complete timesheet lines are entity: TimesheetLine chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Daily hours charged to project and pay code. For each optional field, how many timesheet lines leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'project' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'wbs node', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE wbs_node_id IS NULL) FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'cost code', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE cost_code_id IS NULL) FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'labor rate', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE labor_rate IS NULL) FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'labor cost', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE labor_cost IS NULL) FROM bus_timesheet_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
