%%report inventory-transaction-changed-per-month title: Inventory Transactions last changed per month entity: InventoryTransaction chart: line x: month y: records help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. How recently inventory transactions were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report inventory-transaction-age-bands title: How recently inventory transactions were changed entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report inventory-transaction-edit-churn title: How often inventory transactions are edited entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: edits y: records help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Records by how many times they have been saved; the heavily edited ones are where the process is being fought. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN version <= 1 THEN 'never edited' WHEN version <= 3 THEN 'edited once or twice' WHEN version <= 9 THEN 'edited 3 to 8 times' ELSE 'edited 9 or more times' END AS edits, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(version)
%%report inventory-transaction-transaction-date-per-month title: Inventory Transactions by transaction date entity: InventoryTransaction chart: line x: month y: records help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Inventory Transactions grouped by the month of transaction date, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', transaction_date), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND transaction_date IS NOT NULL AND transaction_date >= now() - interval '24 months' AND transaction_date < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report inventory-transaction-quantity-by-transaction-type title: Total quantity by transaction type entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: transaction_type y: total_quantity help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Inventory Transactions added up on quantity, split by transaction type, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(transaction_type::text, '(unset)') AS transaction_type, ROUND(SUM(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS total_quantity FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report inventory-transaction-quantity-per-month title: Average quantity per month (Inventory Transaction) entity: InventoryTransaction chart: line x: month y: average_quantity help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. The average quantity of inventory transactions created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_quantity FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report inventory-transaction-largest-by-quantity title: The ten largest inventory transactions by quantity entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: record y: quantity help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. The records with the highest quantity; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT transaction_number::text AS record, quantity FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND quantity IS NOT NULL ORDER BY quantity DESC LIMIT 10
%%report inventory-transaction-unit-cost-by-transaction-type title: Total unit cost by transaction type entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: transaction_type y: total_unit_cost help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Inventory Transactions added up on unit cost, split by transaction type, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(transaction_type::text, '(unset)') AS transaction_type, ROUND(SUM(unit_cost)::numeric, 2) AS total_unit_cost FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report inventory-transaction-unit-cost-per-month title: Average unit cost per month (Inventory Transaction) entity: InventoryTransaction chart: line x: month y: average_unit_cost help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. The average unit cost of inventory transactions created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(unit_cost)::numeric, 2) AS average_unit_cost FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report inventory-transaction-largest-by-unit-cost title: The ten largest inventory transactions by unit cost entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: record y: unit_cost help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. The records with the highest unit cost; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT transaction_number::text AS record, unit_cost FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND unit_cost IS NOT NULL ORDER BY unit_cost DESC LIMIT 10
%%report inventory-transaction-per-item title: Inventory Transactions per item entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: item y: records help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Which item the most inventory transactions belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.item_code::text, '(none)') AS item, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_inventory_transaction x LEFT JOIN bus_item p ON p.id = x.item_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report inventory-transaction-quantity-per-item title: Total quantity per item (Inventory Transaction) entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: item y: total_quantity help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. Inventory Transactions added up on quantity for each item, ten largest first. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.item_code::text, '(none)') AS item, ROUND(SUM(x.quantity)::numeric, 2) AS total_quantity FROM bus_inventory_transaction x LEFT JOIN bus_item p ON p.id = x.item_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 10
%%report inventory-transaction-completeness title: How complete inventory transactions are entity: InventoryTransaction chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Receipt, issue, transfer, return or adjustment of inventory. For each optional field, how many inventory transactions leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'from warehouse' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE from_warehouse_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'to warehouse', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE to_warehouse_id IS NULL) FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'project', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE project_id IS NULL) FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'wbs node', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE wbs_node_id IS NULL) FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'cost code', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE cost_code_id IS NULL) FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'journal line', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE journal_line_id IS NULL) FROM bus_inventory_transaction WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
